  "summary": "ACCEPT with no Critical, High, or Constitution MUST finding. The design uses exhaustive typed Pass 1/Pass 2 job and result unions; verifies an authorized committed-revision source slice and both hashes before provider execution; reuses the existing encrypted System/global Worker Agent assignment without credentials in contracts or evidence; applies bounded streaming JSON preflight plus closed deserialization and semantic validation; maps valid results through the existing authorization-scoped KnowledgeCommit boundary before durable progress; dispatches exactly one prepared Pass 2 job only at Pass1Completed; requires set-equal GENERATED_FROM provenance while making narrative-derived base REFERENCES unrepresentable; corrects F003 with a real two-context SQLite reservation regression before production DI; requires no migration; and assigns current-boundary integration to Story 11.3 while preserving the clean-database two-Repository and Docker checks for Story 11.5. The planned-change section accurately identifies both mandatory triggers and cites the applicable PRD and accepted August 15 authority. The accepted plan therefore advances to the single required planned-change authorization checkpoint before task generation; this verdict does not duplicate or waive that authorization."
